🏭 PRODUCTION-LIKE BENCHMARK SUITE 🏭
Three scenarios to find out WHERE each cache actually fits, not just which is fastest overall.

This will take a few minutes (multiple trials x 3 scenarios x 5 caches).

================================================================
SCENARIO A — Realistic Mixed Workload (80% GET / 20% INSERT, Zipfian hot keys)
================================================================
Key space: 200,000 | Cache capacity: 50,000 (forces real eviction)
Zipfian exponent 1.1 — a small set of keys gets most of the traffic,
mirroring real cache access patterns (hot users, hot API routes, hot DNS names).

Cache            Total (ms)            GET p99         INSERT p99     Hit rate
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PulseMap           165.3ms          967ns ± 36ns             1.057µs ± 45ns            91.3%
Moka               400.7ms        3.022µs ± 329ns           75.127µs ± 2.251µs         91.7%
QuickCache         112.7ms          550ns ± 142ns              578ns ± 157ns           91.7%
LRU                461.8ms       28.060µs ± 3.324µs         28.030µs ± 3.191µs         91.7%
Simple             350.2ms       19.028µs ± 416ns           19.229µs ± 570ns           91.7%

================================================================
SCENARIO B — Large Scale: 5M inserts, 200K capacity, memory footprint
================================================================
Single-threaded, constant heavy eviction (cache is 2.5% of insert volume).
Measures RSS growth (actual memory cost per cache design), not just speed.

Cache            Total (ms) Throughput (ops/s)   RSS delta (MB)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
PulseMap           967.7ms            5167128            0.0MB
Moka             15873.6ms             314988            4.5MB
QuickCache        1225.7ms            4079350            0.0MB
LRU               1068.9ms            4677858            0.0MB
Simple            1171.8ms            4267062           77.9MB

Note: RSS delta is a coarse proxy (process-wide, includes allocator/OS noise).
Trust the relative ordering more than the absolute MB numbers.

================================================================
SCENARIO C — Extreme Hot-Key Contention (64 keys, 8 threads, 50/50 GET/INSERT)
================================================================
Isolates lock/contention cost from eviction cost: tiny keyspace means
every thread is constantly touching the same handful of buckets/locks.

Cache            Total (ms)        p99 latency
--------------------------------------------------
PulseMap           233.4ms        1.074µs ± 79ns     
Moka               951.4ms       51.695µs ± 3.803µs  
QuickCache         107.3ms          790ns ± 264ns    
LRU                255.5ms        7.961µs ± 3.990µs  
Simple             320.4ms       11.483µs ± 1.750µs  

================================================================
Done. Read the three sections above — a cache that wins Scenario A
(hot-key mixed traffic) but loses Scenario C (extreme contention)
tells you something different than one that wins everywhere.
